data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** The syntax is straightforward:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

This works without `unsafe` — the `Span<T>` assignment keeps it safe. On this 64-bit system, each element is 8 bytes; on a 32-bit runtime it would be 4 bytes.
